CORE
main.c
--constant-array-oob-nondet
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] .* equal indices, equal elements: FAILURE$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] .* in bounds: an operand: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] .* not every operand is 1: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
array_ackermann_constant with --constant-array-oob-nondet: two out-of-bounds
reads at the same index may now differ (assertion 1 fails), in-bounds reads
still see their operand (assertion 2 holds). Without the option assertion 1
holds; that is array_ackermann_constant.
The array is sized above MAX_FLATTENED_ARRAY_SIZE bits, so it goes through
the array theory (arrayst), not flattening.
